{%- comment -%}
  CAVIERA global loader — the Living Oryx (2026-08-18 unification).

  This is now the ONE loading language for the whole theme: a full-screen, silent, looping Oryx
  video on a solid Cinnabar (#8F261F) field, shown for genuine internal full-page navigation waits
  (e.g. homepage → The House / Journal / Craftsmanship / Our Diamonds / Bespoke / Client Care), and
  nothing else. It replaces two previously separate systems: a one-off "THE HOUSE" ceremonial
  trigger that always played the full video to completion regardless of how long the real
  navigation actually took, and a separate Cinnabar/House-Seal "Curtain" overlay used for every
  other internal link. Both are retired — see assets/caviera-loader.js for the single navigation-
  interception + reveal/conceal engine that replaces them, and assets/caviera-loader.css for the
  visual states.

  Rendered globally (every page, not homepage-only) since qualifying navigation can begin from
  anywhere. The root element always renders unconditionally when settings.enable_loader is on; the
  script decides at runtime whether/when to actually reveal it — a blocked/failed script, or a
  navigation that never needs it, never overlays or blocks any page.

  Video: autoplay + loop natively (the walk repeats for as long as a wait is genuinely still in
  progress — never tied to the video's own runtime), muted (audio is never enabled), playsinline
  (never opens a native fullscreen player on iOS), preload="auto" (the loader is meant to be able to
  reveal instantly the moment it's needed). No controls, no poster frame, no text, no percentage.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.enable_loader -%}
  <div class="caviera-loader" data-caviera-loader aria-hidden="true">
    <video
      class="caviera-loader__video"
      data-loader-video
      src="{{ 'caviera-loader-oryx-2026.mp4' | asset_url }}"
      autoplay
      muted
      loop
      playsinline
      preload="auto"
    ></video>
  </div>
  <script src="{{ 'caviera-loader.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}
